{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/65246-what-does-epic-attributes-represent-both-editions-i-suppose","id":65246,"title":"What does Epic Attributes represent? (Both editions I suppose)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-04T17:19:05-08:00","id":65246,"title":"What does Epic Attributes represent? (Both editions I suppose)","content":"What does Epic Attributes actually represent? What do they <i>do </i>to your character?<br /> <br /> Are they like Aberrants Mega-Attributes? Where even only one dot is supposed to represent a greater ability than any normal human being can ever possess. Not that this was supported by Aberrants rules, a normal human with attribute 5 consistently outdid an aberrant with attribute 2 and Mega-Attribute 1 (except for strength, who was the odd man out).<br /> <br /> Or are they more like 'your ability is raised with (automatic successes)x2', so that a scion with attribute 2 and Epic Attribute 2 basically has 'attribute 6'?<br /> <br /> Or do they represent some sort of influence of events, that the world somehow bends to make things easier for you?<br /> <br /> Or can you chose any of the above to be true for your character?<br /> <br /> So if your scion has appearance 2 and Epic Appearance 1 (the attractive variant), does this make him/her more attractive than any mortal can be? Or 'just' pretty dang attractive (the equivalent of appearance 4) or just a normal looking guy/gal who somehow has more 'luck' with appearance rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","name":"Gammelbraxen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T17:58:46-08:00","id":65276,"title":"","content":"Couching this in the classic &quot;Your mileage may vary&quot; terms, but Epic attributes are just that.<br /> <br /> Having even a single rank will, under normal circumstances, prevent botches and guarantee success at most tasks (hooray auto-successes).<br /> A scion with mediocre attributes but a single Epic may be outstripped by a mortal with 5 dots in the same attribute and whatever ability you are using. That's simple math. It also reflects the early game - you are just a touch better than mortal men. What Epics give you that (arguably) Mega-Attributes do not, is that they open the door to knacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T20:40:39-08:00","id":65361,"title":"","content":"I think the real problem that they had a lot of people wanted is all the 'effects' of Epic Attributes, but not let it so heavily skew dice rolls.<br /> <br /> There were some really awful write ups in God. Legend 9 titanspawn that I'm sure my Legend 6ish players could have probably trampled hard. I mean, no epic attributes and a 12 dice damage pool at Legend 9 is... well, really, really bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T23:10:43-08:00","id":65439,"title":"","content":"Had some interesting discussions with a player about this, in terms of what EAs actually <i>do</i> to a Scion's body. The example in question had to do with hormone-based birth control and Epic Stamina, but I think that the concept of Epic Attributes can bring up a whole host of interesting conundrums. For example, does a character with Epic STR accidentally break stuff by applying too much force sometimes? stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T06:49:13-08:00","id":65636,"title":"","content":"As I recall reading, this is SCIon, not SCIence. We are supposed to be talking of gods. The laws of nature only apply if imposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T12:57:14-08:00","id":65891,"title":"","content":"The laws of nature totally apply, especially at Hero, but even getting into higher tiers of power. Not even an Avatar can, say, permanently make gravity a repulsive force rather than an attractive one (gravity, you sexy sexy beast). Someone who has epic attributes is going to have something different going on in their body than someone without.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T13:45:03-08:00","id":65924,"title":"","content":"I only have passing familiarity with Scion, but the way that I always interpreted Epic Attributes?<br /> <br /> They are mythic.<br /> <br /> What do I mean by that? Well, they fulfill some aspect of your character's personal narrative as dictated by his Fate and Ichor. Your character is epically strong because his legend says that he is. Your character is epically intelligent because her legend says that she is. Whatever her intended role in the grand scheme of the story of the gods and their children and their enemies determines what Epic Attributes they develop.<br /> <br /> What does that mean on a personal, sensation level? I, personally, would write it as a sense of overwhelming rightness. Not talent <i>per se</i>, where you have a moment of inspiration and wow yourself, but whenever you tap into your Epic Attributes, things are just <i>right</i>. You are where you need to be in the world. If you're epically strong, then you just feel <i>right</i> when you're lifting or breaking something. If you're epically smart, then you just feel <i>right</i> when you're puzzling out a problem or working out a mystery.<br /> <br /> And so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T14:25:06-08:00","id":65957,"title":"","content":"Something about tossing a supercarrier (over 100k tons) beyond planetary orbit that appeals to me. Of course, if this was physics class, that would be silly, since it would break into pieces with the force of the heave and under it's own weight. (I'm reminded of a comic-book character, &quot;Gladiator&quot; when he <a href=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/0/5187/1499329-624813_fantasticfour_v1_249_p14.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">lifted a skyscraper</a>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T11:50:01-08:00","id":66625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/65246-what-does-epic-attributes-represent-both-editions-i-suppose?p=65891#post65891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even an Avatar can, say, permanently make gravity a repulsive force rather than an attractive one (gravity, you sexy sexy beast).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly the kind of thing certain Avatars can do. You would probably need to get a bunch of other gods to agree with your plan, and assist with their own Avatars, or someone else is going to pop their Avatar and contest you on the matter. But as long as you are only trying to reverse gravity in a relatively limited area (a hundred miles or so) then you will only make a few enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:53:03-08:00","id":66755,"title":"","content":"&quot;Permanently&quot; was the operative word, methinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T16:53:15-08:00","id":66847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/65246-what-does-epic-attributes-represent-both-editions-i-suppose?p=66755#post66755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Permanently&quot; was the operative word, methinks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The things you create with Avatars are permanent, unless you choose otherwise at the time of creation or someone else meddles with them. The Shaper can create mountain ranges, The Flood can create seas, The Storm can create annual weather patterns, and The Green can leave a vast forest of thorns that hunger for the blood of adventurers =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T19:17:22-08:00","id":66903,"title":"","content":"I don't think that permanently changing the underlying rules of the universe in a global sense, applying to all beings, objects, and so forth is within the bailiwick of any avatar. At least, I just went through Scion: God and didn't see anything like that. Avatars and Ultimate Attributes can create incredible, sweeping change, but I don't think it makes sense for them to be able to permanently undermine or rewrite the rules that the universe plays by. You want to raise a mountain range with The Shaper? Sure. That mountain range will change the world's weather in a predictable way, unless you or some other deity takes action. You want to make it so that magnetic poles will have like attracting like instead of opposites attract? I don't think that's the kind of thing that can be done except at the inception of a space. I'd imagine the only time a character can do that is if they were splitting off their own little portion of the overworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T19:29:16-08:00","id":66910,"title":"","content":"*nods* Unless we're talking of &quot;Chaos,&quot; any...<b>thing</b> created will still be subject to physical laws, otherwise they wouldn't be what they are. Hmm...I'm forgetting something I think. Something about rewriting reality....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T19:35:00-08:00","id":66915,"title":"","content":"I mean, it seems pretty simple to me. You can't design a game where all of a sudden all the rules totally change. There has to be some framework to make things at least slightly predictable, or what's the point. For most games, the jumping-off point is that some basic scientific laws apply. More muscle=more force (that's how you get a strength stat). Faster things fly farther (that's why different projectile weapons have different ranges). Et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T21:23:39-08:00","id":66967,"title":"","content":"It really varies from one storyteller to the next. I have seen one storyteller who allowed Avatars to effect universal constants directly. I have seen another storyteller who restricted Avatars to only a set distance. And I have seen a third storyteller give a set distance, but exponentially increase that distance for every other Avatar you have cooperating towards that goal. I probably lie somewhere near the third?<br /> <br /> I have no problem with a dozen or more avatars getting together and building a whole new planet, complete with rules that absolutely defy any scientific explanation for why they are working the way they do. Once you have reached Legend 12, you no longer need to have any kind of framework. You're already a pan dimensional entity who has no doubt visited any number of realms with their individual 'framework' which may or may not differ from that of the mundus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T22:04:14-08:00","id":66988,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I'll be the first to admit that most of what I post on these forums is about how I would run things, and I fully respect the right of other storytellers to run things in a completely different way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T11:48:20-08:00","id":69271,"title":"","content":"I would say that to an extent, Epic Attributes and Knacks bend the natural laws to the point that they are merely suggestions while a Scion is performing a legendary feat. That super strong Scion with Epic Strength doesn't have to worry about ripping the bumper off the truck he is using as a club to pound a Titanspawn into submission... even though structurally that is what Science says should happen when he applies his Epic Strength to a situation. Likewise, the super fast Scion with a ton of Epic Dexterity only creates a sonic boom when running when he desires... and doesn't drag any trash in his wake unless he wants to... and as for his mundane clothing burning up from the friction of air resistance aganst him... doesn't happen... even though Science says they all should happen.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that Scions are permanently re-writing the laws of nature? Of course not... merely that the laws do not apply as strictly to them as they do to mere mortals (or Scions with lesser legends). The higher one's Legend and Epics, the less the established laws bind one. Of course using one's full power will often lead to major fate-bindings... but that goes without saying when one performs feats that fly in the face of what is normally expected... not that the term &quot;normal&quot; really applies to Scions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}